---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="FlyItalyADSB is Italy's first ADS-B flight tracking community. A community run by enthusiasts, infrastructure by Nesso Labs."
>
  <div class="pt-24 pb-20 px-6 sm:px-12 lg:px-20 max-w-4xl mx-auto">

    <div class="mb-14">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">Project</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">About</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-lg">
        FlyItalyADSB is Italy's first ADS-B flight tracking community.
        Started in 2020 as Riccardo Sabatti's passion project, it has grown into a data collection
        infrastructure with global coverage and applications in scientific research.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Values -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <div class="tag-row">
        <span><b>Community</b> · volunteers + Nesso Labs · map and Free API plan at no cost, paid plans help cover the costs</span>
        <span><b>Unfiltered data</b> · no FAA/LADD/BARR, military included via MLAT</span>
        <span><b>Open source</b> · readsb/tar1090/mlat-server, all freely reusable</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- History -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-8">History</h2>
      <div class="timeline">
        <div class="row">
          <span class="dot"></span><span class="year">2020</span>
          <div>
            <p>
              <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/riccardo-sabatti/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-sky-400 no-underline hover:text-sky-300">Riccardo Sabatti</a> set up a first ADS-B antenna and started sharing its data with ADS-B Exchange.
              That was the beginning of FlyItalyADSB.
            </p>
            <div class="photos">
              <figure>
                <a href="/img/storia/2020-antenna.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/img/storia/2020-antenna.jpg" alt="The vertical antenna mounted on the receiver box" width="900" height="1600" loading="lazy" style="object-position:50% 100%" /></a>
                <figcaption>July 2020 · the antenna on the receiver box</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <figure>
                <a href="/img/storia/2020-ricevitore.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/img/storia/2020-ricevitore.jpg" alt="Inside the box: Raspberry Pi, 1090 MHz preamp and fan" width="775" height="1600" loading="lazy" /></a>
                <figcaption>July 2020 · inside: Raspberry Pi, 1090 MHz preamp, fan</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <figure>
                <a href="/img/storia/2020-copertura.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/img/storia/2020-copertura.jpg" alt="The Virtual Radar Server map on a laptop, with the first aircraft received" width="664" height="1182" loading="lazy" /></a>
                <figcaption>October 2020 · the first aircraft received, on Virtual Radar Server</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <figure>
                <a href="/img/storia/2020-dicembre.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/img/storia/2020-dicembre.jpg" alt="A complete receiver inside a weatherproof box" width="768" height="1024" loading="lazy" /></a>
                <figcaption>December 2020 · a receiver in its box</figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="dot"></span><span class="year">2021</span>
          <div>
            <p>
              In early 2021 flyitalyadsb.com went online: a live map, a script to share your own antenna,
              and MLAT. Each antenna receives aircraft up to 400 km away. The network grew across central and
              northern Italy.
            </p>
            <div class="photos">
              <figure>
                <a href="/img/storia/2021-sito.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/img/storia/2021-sito.jpg" alt="The first flyitalyadsb.com home page on a phone" width="615" height="1168" loading="lazy" style="object-position:50% 0%" /></a>
                <figcaption>January 2021 · the first flyitalyadsb.com home page</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <figure>
                <a href="/img/storia/2021-mappa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/img/storia/2021-mappa.jpg" alt="The tar1090 map with aircraft over northern Italy" width="615" height="1064" loading="lazy" /></a>
                <figcaption>January 2021 · the tar1090 map over northern Italy</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <figure>
                <a href="/img/storia/2021-mondo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/img/storia/2021-mondo.jpg" alt="The map zoomed out: every aircraft is over Italy" width="923" height="1600" loading="lazy" /></a>
                <figcaption>January 2021 · zoomed out, the whole network fits in Italy</figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="dot"></span><span class="year">2023</span>
          <p>
            By then the map covered from Sweden to Basilicata and from south-eastern France to the Czech Republic.
            In January JETNET, an aviation data company controlled by the fund Silversmith Capital Partners,
            bought ADS-B Exchange, and the open tracking community fragmented. FlyItalyADSB maintained its independence
            and positioned itself alongside new community players such as adsb.lol, adsb.fi
            and airplanes.live — all based on the same open source stack, all unfiltered.
            In May it joined the aggregators offered by <a href="https://adsb.im" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-sky-400 no-underline hover:text-sky-300">adsb.im</a>, the receiver software image that feeds several networks at once.
            With the sale of ADS-B Exchange and with adsb.im, FlyItalyADSB went global.
            In October a collaboration with adsb.lol began, with the two networks exchanging data, MLAT included.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="dot"></span><span class="year">2025</span>
          <p>
            Mode-S data collected by the network became the foundation of the
            <a href="/en/research/weather" class="text-sky-400 no-underline hover:text-sky-300">weather32</a>
            meteorological research project, which uses aircraft as high-altitude wind sensors
            to validate ERA5 reanalyses and IASI profiles.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="dot"></span><span class="year">2026</span>
          <p>
            In late August the <a href="/en/data/api" class="text-sky-400 no-underline hover:text-sky-300">public API</a> and the MCP server launched:
            the network's data can be queried from code or from an AI agent such as Claude.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <span class="dot"></span><span class="year">Today</span>
          <p>
            Coverage is global: beyond the Italian receivers, direct feeders across Europe,
            the Americas, Asia and Oceania extend the map worldwide.
            Over Italy the network computes MLAT unfiltered, including military flights.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Nesso Labs -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-6">Infrastructure</h2>
      <div class="p-6 rounded-xl border flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6 items-start" style="background:#0f1929;border-color:#1e3048">
        <div class="flex-1">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-2">Nesso Labs</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            FlyItalyADSB relies on Nesso Labs for hosting and servers.
            Thanks to Nesso Labs for its support.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Contacts -->
    <section id="contatti" class="scroll-mt-20">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-6">Contact</h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-8">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border" style="background:#0f1929;border-color:#1e3048">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-200 mb-1 text-sm">Research inquiries</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Bulk extractions from the history (many aircraft or long periods) — for university or institutional research.
          </p>
          <a href="mailto:info@flyitalyadsb.com" class="text-sm text-sky-400 no-underline hover:text-sky-300">info@flyitalyadsb.com</a>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border" style="background:#0f1929;border-color:#1e3048">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-200 mb-1 text-sm">GitHub</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Source code for custom components: readsb fork, mlat-server, flarm-ogn-to-sbs.
          </p>
          <a href="https://github.com/flyitalyadsb" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-sm text-sky-400 no-underline hover:text-sky-300">github.com/flyitalyadsb ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="p-6 rounded-xl border" style="background:#0a1320;border-color:#1e3048">
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          For general questions, feeder setup support or other requests, see the
          <a href="/en/contact" class="text-sky-400 no-underline">Contact us</a> page.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</Layout>
